A single string literal longer than the line limit, assigned on one line.
Strings are never split, so the line stays long; the scenario pins that
the wrap pass leaves an unbreakable statement alone.
-- input.ssl --
:DECLARE sNote;
sNote := "This string literal is deliberately very long so that it exceeds every sensible maximum line length setting by a wide margin";
:RETURN sNote;
-- format [--max-line-length 40] --
